<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Carson lifts shr for nine months to end Dec.</title>
<headline>Carson lifts shr for nine months to end Dec.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nine months ended December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     17.0	  vs    14.4</p>
<p>    Retained income	 6.23	  vs    5.77</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   9.48	  vs    9.09</p>
<p>    Tax			 3.26	  vs    3.33</p>
<p>    Interest received     0.87	  vs    1.16</p>
<p>    Turnover		 39.91	  vs   40.30</p>
<p>Full name: Carson Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The directors have resolved to award capitalisation shares to ordinary shareholders registered in the books of the company on March 28 1997 in the ratio of 0.36 new fully paid ordinary shares for every 100 paid.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
